                >
                    <p
                        class="font-bold text-red-800 text-sm uppercase tracking-wide mb-1"
                    >
                        ⚠️ Update (November 2026)
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-red-900 font-medium">
                        BC PNP's 2026 allocation is <strong>6,254 nominations</strong>: 5,254 confirmed in December 2025 plus 1,000 added on August 18, 2026, still well below the 9,000 requested. Since April 23, 2026, invitations are organized around Care, Build and Innovate, the separate tech draws have ended, and the Entry Level and Semi-Skilled stream is closed. Sections of this guide written in early 2026 have been updated where facts changed. See the <a href="/bc-pnp-draws" class="underline font-bold">latest BC PNP draws</a> for current cutoffs.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <h2>What's New in 2026?</h2>
                <p>
                    The BC PNP landscape for 2026 is dramatically different from
                    previous years. On December 18, 2025, Immigration, Refugees
                    and Citizenship Canada (IRCC) confirmed British Columbia's
                    allocation for the year: <strong>5,254 nominations</strong>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    This is a stark contrast to the 9,000 nominations BC
                    requested to meet its labor market needs. While this
                    represents a 31% increase from the <em>initial</em> 4,000 nominations
                    granted in early 2025, it's actually <strong
                        >nearly 1,000 fewer</strong
                    > than the 6,214 nominations BC ultimately received throughout
                    2025 after mid-year top-ups. On August 18, 2026, IRCC added
                    1,000 nominations, bringing BC's 2026 allocation to
                    <strong>6,254</strong>.
                </p>

                <h2>2025 vs 2026: Key Differences</h2>
                <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6">
                    <table class="min-w-full text-left text-sm">
                        <thead class="bg-slate-100 border-b-2 border-slate-200">
                            <tr>
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 font-black text-slate-900"
                                    >Aspect</th
                                >
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 font-black text-slate-900"
                                    >2025</th
                                >
                                <th class="px-4 py-3 font-black text-slate-900"
                                    >2026</th
                                >
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold"
                                    >Initial Allocation</td
                                >
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">4,000</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">5,254</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold"
                                    >Final Allocation</td
                                >
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">6,214 (after top-ups)</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-red-600 font-bold"
                                    >6,254 (after Aug 18 top-up)</td
                                >
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold"
                                    >Student Streams</td
                                >
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">Suspended April 2025</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-red-600"
                                    >Will not launch (Apr 23)</td
                                >
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
