                <h2>Stream Status for 2026</h2>

                <h3 id="streams">
                    ✅ Skills Immigration (Skilled Worker, Health Authority)
                </h3>
                <p>
                    The Skilled Worker and Health Authority streams remain open;
                    the Entry Level and Semi-Skilled (ELSS) stream is closed
                    (announced April 23, 2026). However,
                    with limited allocations, BC PNP is prioritizing candidates
                    with <strong>high economic impact</strong>—meaning higher
                    wages, in-demand occupations, and regional connections
                    matter more than ever. Learn more in our <a href="/articles/bc-pnp-skilled-worker-stream" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Skilled Worker Stream guide</a> or <a href="/articles/bc-pnp-entry-level-semi-skilled" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">ELSS guide</a> (now closed).
                </p>

                <h3 id="tech">❌ BC PNP Tech draws (ended)</h3>
                <p>
                    The separate BC PNP Tech draws for <a href="/articles/bc-pnp-tech-stream-occupations" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">priority
                    technology occupations</a> have ended. Tech workers with a
                    qualifying B.C. job offer can still be invited through Innovate:
                    High Economic Impact rounds, either by wage ($49/hr and
                    $99,000/yr in the October 29, 2026 round) or by points (cutoff
                    131). See our <a href="/articles/tech-workers-bc-pnp-2027-after-tech-draws-ended" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">guide for tech workers after the tech draws ended</a>.
                </p>

                <div
                    class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-400 p-4 my-6 not-prose rounded-r-xl"
                >
                    <p
                        class="font-bold text-blue-800 text-sm uppercase tracking-wide mb-1"
                    >
                        💡 Tech Tip
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-blue-900 font-medium">
                        If you have a high-paying tech job offer, check it against
                        the latest Innovate wage threshold. Wage-based invitations
                        do not depend on your overall registration score.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <h3 id="health">✅ Healthcare Priority</h3>
                <p>
                    Healthcare professionals remain a top priority for BC PNP.
                    Nurses, physicians, and allied health workers with valid job
                    offers are invited in Care: Health rounds (minimum score 76
                    in September and October 2026), and health authority
                    employees can apply directly under the Health Authority
                    stream. See our <a href="/articles/bc-pnp-health-authority-stream" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Health Authority Stream guide</a> for details.
                </p>

                <h3>❌ Student/Graduate Streams</h3>
                <p>
                    The new Bachelor's, Master's, and Doctorate streams
                    announced in late 2024 have been <strong
                        >indefinitely suspended</strong
                    > since April 2025, and on April 23, 2026 BC said it will not
                    launch new student streams. The legacy International
                    Post-Graduate (IPG) stream closed on January 7, 2025.
                </p>

                <div
                    class="bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 my-6 not-prose rounded-r-xl"
                >
                    <p
                        class="font-bold text-yellow-800 text-sm uppercase tracking-wide mb-1"
                    >
                        ⚠️ For International Graduates
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-yellow-900 font-medium">
                        If you recently graduated from a BC institution, your
                        current option is the <strong>Skilled Worker</strong> stream—which
                        requires a qualifying job offer in NOC TEER 0 to 3 and two
                        years of skilled work experience. BC said on April 23, 2026
                        that it will not launch new student streams, although B.C.
                        study still earns extra registration points.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <h2>Strategies to Maximize Your Chances in 2026</h2>

                <h3>1. Focus on High-Wage Job Offers</h3>
                <p>
                    The BC PNP SIRS (Skills Immigration Registration System)
                    heavily weights your <strong>wage</strong>. A job offer
                    paying $30–40/hour or more significantly boosts your score
                    compared to minimum wage positions.
                </p>

                <h3>2. Target Priority Occupations</h3>
                <p>
                    Care occupations (health, childcare, education and veterinary
                    care) and Build construction trades are explicitly
                    prioritized, and high earners can be invited through Innovate
                    wage rounds. If you have transferable skills, consider
                    pivoting to positions in these sectors.
                </p>

                <h3>3. Consider Regional Locations</h3>
                <p>
                    Jobs outside Metro Vancouver receive additional points in
                    the SIRS system. Communities in the Interior, Northern BC,
                    and Vancouver Island may offer both lower competition and
                    higher scores. See our <a href="/articles/bc-pnp-regional-priorities" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Regional Priorities guide</a> for city-by-city breakdowns.
                </p>

                <h3>4. Improve Your Language Scores</h3>
                <p>
                    Higher CLB scores translate directly to more points. If
                    you're at CLB 7, consider retaking IELTS or CELPIP to reach
                    CLB 8 or 9—it can make the difference between invitation and
                    waiting. Learn more in our <a href="/articles/bc-pnp-language-requirements" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Language Requirements guide</a>.
                </p>

                <h3>5. Stay Ready to Move Fast</h3>
                <p>
                    BC PNP holds rounds about monthly, and invitations can come quickly.
                    Ensure your BCPNP Online profile is complete, your <a href="/articles/bc-pnp-documents-checklist" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">documents
                    are up-to-date</a>, and you're ready to submit within the 30-calendar-day
                    deadline.
                </p>

