                                >▼</span
                            >
                        </summary>
                        <div
                            class="mt-4 text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-slate-100 pt-4 animate-fadeIn"
                        >
                            Yes. If you have a valid Express Entry profile and
                            receive a BC PNP nomination, you can apply through
                            the Express Entry BC (EEBC) option. The January 5,
                            2026 federal draw issued 574 ITAs to PNP candidates
                            with a CRS of 711, and the October 13 and 26 PNP
                            rounds had cutoffs of 772 and 761. IRCC's revised CRS
                            took effect on November 3, 2026, and rounds were
                            paused while profiles were rescored. You should also look into dedicated pathways for those already inside the country like the <a href="/articles/canada-tr-to-pr-pathway-2026" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">2026 TR to PR Pathway</a>.
                        </div>
