        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8 mt-12">
            <section class="bg-white p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">2026 Allocation and Why Cut-Offs Are Higher</h2>
                <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                    The federal 2025-2027 Immigration Levels Plan cut the national PNP target from 110,000 in 2024 to 55,000 in 2025. The 2026-2028 plan raised it to 91,500 for 2026, and the 2027-2029 plan, released on November 5, 2026, sets 95,000 a year. BC's 2026 allocation is 6,254 nominations (5,254 confirmed in December 2025 plus 1,000 added on August 18, 2026), against the 9,000 it requested. That scarcity is the single biggest force pushing SIRS cut-off scores upward.
                </p>
                <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                    BC PNP responded by tightening targeted draws, prioritizing healthcare, childcare/early childhood educators, veterinary care, construction trades, and a small "high economic priority" category covering specific in-demand professionals. Since April 23, 2026, rounds are organized around Care, Build and Innovate. BC has not published a breakdown of nominations by objective; the estimates below were made in early 2026, before that restructuring, and the tech, International Graduate and Entry-Level categories no longer exist:
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-700">
                    <li>2,400 nominations reserved for healthcare-related streams</li>
                    <li>1,800 for tech-targeted draws</li>
                    <li>1,200 for early childhood educators and childcare workers</li>
                    <li>900 for construction trades</li>
                    <li>1,000 for general Skilled Worker and EEBC draws combined</li>
                    <li>700 for International Graduate, Entry-Level and Semi-Skilled, and other streams</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
                    Numbers shift quarter to quarter. Check the <a href="/articles/canada-immigration-levels-plan-2026-2028-bc-pnp-impact" class="text-red-600 underline">Immigration Levels Plan analysis</a> for the latest updates.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="bg-white p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Stream-by-Stream Snapshot</h2>
                <div class="overflow-x-auto">
                    <table class="min-w-full text-left text-sm">
